Notebook[{
Cell["Numerical check of the five-point monodromy relations", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"8b61296e-5ec8-421f-9b6a-de622ea8a1a7"],

Cell["\<\
All 25 monodromy relations produced by monodromyRelations5pt.nb are checked \
numerically at a single kinematic point, by evaluating the 100 Z-integrals \
they contain and substituting.

Nothing outside Mathematica is needed: no NCAlgebra, no PolyLogTools, no HPL, \
no ginsh.  zNumerics.m is plain Wolfram Language -- every multiple \
polylogarithm appearing at weight 2 has an elementary closed form, which is \
what makes the 10^4-10^6 integrand samples per integral affordable.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d3306bf7-dd9c-47e0-8ba9-8c872b333017"],

Cell["Load", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"72a1e537-16fb-4833-bfb1-59bc0acc8c16"],

Cell["\<\
nbDir = NotebookDirectory[];
Get[FileNameJoin[{nbDir, \"zNumerics.m\"}]];
monData = Get[FileNameJoin[{nbDir, \"monEqs5_W2.m\"}]];

zList = Union@Cases[monData[\"equations\"][[All, 2]], _Zc, Infinity];

Column[{
  Row[{\"weight truncation  : \", monData[\"Wmax\"]}],
  Row[{\"Parke-Taylor order : \", monData[\"rho\"]}],
  Row[{\"relations          : \", Length[monData[\"equations\"]]}],
  Row[{\"distinct Z's       : \", Length[zList]}],
  Row[{\"packages loaded    : \",
       If[Names[\"NCAlgebra`*\"] === {} && Names[\"PolyLogTools`*\"] === {},
          \"none - stock kernel\", \"NCAlgebra / PolyLogTools present\"]}]}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"24d18584-3812-46b1-8059-2918f13b85dc"],

Cell["The kinematic point", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a0a99152-7817-4ea9-b62d-1712b96e5a29"],

Cell["\<\
The relation mixes the four chambers 12345, 13245, 13425 and 21345, so the \
Mandelstam point must sit inside the domain of convergence of all four at \
once.  Reading the facet exponents off the puncture collisions and demanding \
every one exceed -1 gives

    s12, s23, s34, s45, s15 > 0        and        s13, s24, s25 > -1.

This is a real constraint, not a formality.  The single-chamber point {1/5, \
3/10, 3/10, 6/5, 6/5} used earlier satisfies the first group but has s25 = \
-11/5, and the two chambers it misses come back as 10^7 and 10^33.  The point \
below clears all eight conditions; the appendix reads the facet exponents off \
the integrand rather than taking that on trust.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4f0ab308-4f2c-4a21-83a3-d20fec5b80c2"],

Cell["\<\
(* {s12, s23, s34, s45, s15} *)
sMon = {1/5, 3/10, 2/5, 3/5, 7/20};

Grid[Prepend[
  Join[Transpose[{sBasis5, sMon}],
       {#, toBasis5[#] /. sChoice[sMon]} & /@ {s[1, 3], s[2, 4], s[2, 5], \
s[1, 4], s[3, 5]}],
  {\"invariant\", \"value\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"63e4c93e-1304-43e4-99c4-e8cfcf85cc28"],

Cell["The 100 Z-integrals", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"89060241-57e1-4c32-a1a1-a1e43361b551"],

Cell["\<\
(* a few minutes: 100 integrals, each split into 5 sector-decomposed pieces \
*)
{tZ, zVals} = AbsoluteTiming[
   Association[(# -> ZNum[Sequence @@ (List @@ #), sMon][\"value\"]) & /@ \
zList]];

maxZ = Max[Abs[N[Values[zVals]]]];

Column[{
  Row[{\"evaluated \", Length[zVals], \" integrals in \", Round[tZ, 0.1], \" \
s\"}],
  Row[{\"failures : \", Count[Values[zVals], $Failed]}],
  Row[{\"max |Z|  : \", maxZ}],
  Grid[Prepend[{First[#], NumberForm[N[Last[#]], 12]} & /@ Normal[zVals],
       {\"Z\", \"value\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"41da04e1-b82b-4838-83ad-bc554d9bedb6"],

Cell["The 25 residuals", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d98bd46d-75d3-4ed3-b4d0-d4b29fedd26a"],

Cell["\<\
Each relation is a linear combination of Z-integrals with coefficients in the \
Mandelstam invariants; numS puts the coefficients on the independent basis \
and substitutes the point, so a relation that holds returns zero.  What is \
left is quadrature error.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c8cdeb6e-c0e5-4963-af6e-04888e641673"],

Cell["\<\
resid = Table[numS[monData[\"equations\"][[k, 2]] /. zVals, sMon],
              {k, Length[monData[\"equations\"]]}];

Grid[Prepend[
  SortBy[Table[{monData[\"equations\"][[k, 1]], Abs[resid[[k]]], \
Abs[resid[[k]]]/maxZ},
               {k, Length[resid]}], -#[[2]] &],
  {\"basis word\", \"|residual|\", \"relative\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> \
Left]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e024a02f-d63f-4dec-8a74-513034aff5f8"],

Cell["\<\
Column[{
  Row[{\"relations checked      : \", Length[resid]}],
  Row[{\"worst |residual|       : \", Max[Abs[resid]]}],
  Row[{\"best  |residual|       : \", Min[Abs[resid]]}],
  Row[{\"worst relative to |Z|  : \", Max[Abs[resid]]/maxZ}]}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"221dee61-828a-4fb8-8b1c-402d0935d3d5"],

Cell["Appendix: where the kinematic point comes from", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"12612486-ed3c-4dd4-b457-b1a2fc24197b"],

Cell["\<\
The convergence conditions above are not asserted -- they can be read \
straight off the integrand.  convExponents sector-decomposes the integrand of \
a chamber symbolically and takes the limit at each facet, returning the \
exponent the integrand vanishes (or blows up) with there.  Convergence is \
exactly the statement that every one of them exceeds -1.

This cell takes a few minutes: Simplify and Limit on the full symbolic \
integrand, four times over.  It is a check, not a prerequisite -- everything \
above runs without it.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6d087c5f-170a-4767-843e-3c255c6d0550"],

Cell["\<\
(* Read the facet exponents off the sector-decomposed integrand rather than
   asserting them.  Every exponent must exceed -1 for the integral to converge.
   Around 30 s per chamber: Simplify and Limit on the full symbolic \
integrand. *)
facets = Association[(# -> convExponents[#, {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}]) & /@ \
monChambers];

expsAt[ch_] := toBasis5[Flatten[Values /@ Values[facets[ch]]]] /. \
sChoice[sMon];

Grid[Prepend[
  {StringJoin[ToString /@ #], Min[expsAt[#]], TrueQ[Min[expsAt[#]] > -1]} & \
/@ monChambers,
  {\"chamber\", \"worst facet exponent\", \"converges\"}], Frame -> All, \
Alignment -> Left]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"20615375-94ac-4166-86ab-7a8f70058165"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Linux x86 (64-bit) (July 2, 2026)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"a4c5e561-0b77-403d-b23f-545acf70d799"
]
